{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423060-rip-favorite-aberrant-characters-who-are-no-more","id":1423060,"title":"RIP- Favorite Aberrant Characters who are no more","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-11T08:22:14-08:00","id":1423060,"title":"RIP- Favorite Aberrant Characters who are no more","content":"What characters are you personally missing from the new addition, it seems like several may not exist anymore. Sorry if this was posted long ago...<br /> <br /> I miss Shrapnel, Epoch, Sloppy Joe, Dr. Worm (and many others)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:33:00-08:00","id":1423063,"title":"","content":"Sloppy Joe was in the Teragen book, wasn't he? So, he's not missing from the core book. (He's the only one I recognize by name.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T08:36:27-08:00","id":1423065,"title":"","content":"None of those were in the original core book from what I remember, so they could easily still show up later. I'm not really a big fan of Epoch or Dr. Worm, but Shrapnel and Sloppy Joe have always been personal favorites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T10:35:16-08:00","id":1423078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423060-rip-favorite-aberrant-characters-who-are-no-more#post1423060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What characters are you personally missing from the new addition, it seems like several may not exist anymore. Sorry if this was posted long ago...<br /> <br /> I miss Shrapnel, Epoch, Sloppy Joe, Dr. Worm (and many others)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe all of those characters were established in supplements, not the core rules, with the possible exception of Dr. Worm.<br /> <br /> The new edition's rulebook doesn't include them either, but that doesn't mean they don't exist: we can't cover the entirety of 1st Editon's nova roster within the core rulebook, or there'd be no room for the actual game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T15:47:31-08:00","id":1423127,"title":"","content":"Is Natalya 'Swarm Queen' Dornova still around in this edition? She intrigued me in that her powers were a complete mystery, and as the one member of the Teragen 'Pantheon' to be said to be at the famous meeting, and not show up in the 'Last Supper' picture or get a tiny write-up blurb of her own. Homonculos to become a living swarm? Control others through mega-socials to be 'queen bee?' Big scary alien-queen insectoid form and /or quantum clone? Quantum summoning to create 'swarms?' All of the above? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like she, Caroline Fong and Feathered Serpent were the three 'biggest name' Teragen we didn't get much info on in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> Other frequent name-drops that got (IMO) short shrift; Ana Graca Texeria (all we know is that she could fly into orbit to help rescue a space shuttle), Leland 'Saxon' Cornwall (flying telepath psychoperv?), Mehistophaleez (former Elite, now novox celeb), Borealis (Elite who unmasked 'the Stone Badass!'), Gothic Knight ( Batman?).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T16:02:40-08:00","id":1423133,"title":"","content":"Page 131 you have a short profile of Natalia \u201cSwarm Queen\u201d Dornova.<br /> <br /> Caroline Fong is mentioned in Teragen description.<br /> <br /> Ana Gra\u00e7a Teixeira and Saxon (now Bryan \u201cSaxon\u201d Graham) are mentioned in Utopia description.<br /> <br /> The others I didn\u2019t find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T16:41:46-08:00","id":1423137,"title":"","content":"I am sort of curious how they do Ana's powers in her nova writeup. She was an often mentioned T2M nova while having little known about her powers except we knew she could survive the vacuum of space or the depths of the Marianas trench. I've been featuring her in my own Aberrant campaign, but I'm always curious how other people do it. I'm interested to see how they are done in the Proteus Nova Companion. I hope that many of them are written up like PC's so we can see a lot of examples of how characters are constructed. On the Teragen side I'm quite curious about Caroline Fong since she was essentially a non-entity in the 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T17:09:01-08:00","id":1423144,"title":"","content":"Adaptation Mega-Edge can let one survive both sorts of environments with little difficulty. If she has any other powers I don't know but yeah that would be the main survivability power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T17:19:53-08:00","id":1423148,"title":"","content":"In my game I made her the fastest woman alive, tough as steel, and super strong strong to boot. She flies rather than runs though. My group's speedster is both awestruck and jealous since she combines Capoeira into her fighting prowess along with that sweet sweet mega dex and hyper-movement. I still run a 1st ed game though I am pondering making the switch since scale elegantly solves many of my issues with the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T22:03:21-08:00","id":1423181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423060-rip-favorite-aberrant-characters-who-are-no-more?p=1423127#post1423127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Natalya 'Swarm Queen' Dornova still around in this edition? She intrigued me in that her powers were a complete mystery, and as the one member of the Teragen 'Pantheon' to be said to be at the famous meeting, and not show up in the 'Last Supper' picture or get a tiny write-up blurb of her own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarm Queen was in the Last Supper photo, over towards the left. It's the only illustration of her in 1e, IIRC. <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/Tvho9H0.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/Tvho9H0.jpg</a><br /> <br /> She and her weird hair appear in the illustration on p. 177 of Trinity Continuum: Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gothic Knight ( Batman?). </div> </div> </div>Most of the others got covered by Mateus above. Gothic Knight isn't name-dropped, but he appears perched on a rooftop on p. 248 of TC: Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T00:12:38-08:00","id":1423202,"title":"","content":"Not exactly a character, but I was sad to see the QNA not even get a mention in the minor groups section. Considering who all was in it, the QNA had a hilariously powerful membership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T03:41:20-08:00","id":1423231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423060-rip-favorite-aberrant-characters-who-are-no-more?p=1423202#post1423202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly a character, but I was sad to see the QNA not even get a mention in the minor groups section. Considering who all was in it, the QNA had a hilariously powerful membership.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mentioned a few times elsewhere. For me, the name still conjures up 1e's &quot;there's a gay rapist in the QNA, got to represent the oh so important 'gays as degenerate sexual perverted rapist' trope apparently&quot; and &quot;Skew is a homophobic jackass who uses QNE as a replacement for an obvious f-slur while discussing how a comic artist draws him&quot; memories for me, even though I know the 2e version won't do any of that. Like, seriously, I know there were gay writers on the original and they might have even written those bits, but 1e kinda didn't handle the subject well regardless.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I have absolutely no concerns about Onyx Path's ability to handle queer characters. They're one of the queerest companies out there in terms of freelancers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T04:23:43-08:00","id":1423234,"title":"","content":"QNA is mentioned in the London Fog profile (for sure) and in at least another time.<br /> <br /> About Gothic Knight illustration, I missed him completely, while at same time I remember someone pointing out during the KS campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T07:45:16-08:00","id":1423270,"title":"","content":"Is the Houston Tornado still kicking?<br /> <br /> It seems that they also cut a some Mega-intelligent inventor/mastermind Novas, but I can't seem to remember their names off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T08:00:42-08:00","id":1423271,"title":"","content":"Portman is the only character I'm aware of who was alive in the 1e who is explicitly not in 2e. He was the price the writers had to pay for Slider. Only death can pay for life!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T08:03:20-08:00","id":1423273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423060-rip-favorite-aberrant-characters-who-are-no-more?p=1423271#post1423271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only death can pay for life!</div> </div> </div> </div>A soul for a soul...<br /> Remember S\u00e3o Paulo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T02:05:28-08:00","id":1424210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1423060-rip-favorite-aberrant-characters-who-are-no-more?p=1423234#post1423234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Gothic Knight illustration, I missed him completely, while at same time I remember someone pointing out during the KS campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>He also appears on the cover along the left side of the 'column,' silhouetted against the moon, calling back to a similar image on the 1e core book cover. I think that's what got pointed out in the KS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:25:52-08:00","id":1424329,"title":"","content":"I miss Kimberly Dame. She was already 102 years old when she erupted in 1e, so I suspect she died of old age long before 2e's N-Day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}